-- Migration 26: Google Drive connection (OAuth) singleton record.
-- One Drive account per app instance (single-user/couple app, not
-- multi-tenant - see AGENTS.md). access_token/refresh_token are stored
-- Fernet-encrypted by the DriveConnection domain model
-- (open_notebook/domain/drive_connection.py), using the same encryption
-- helper as AI provider credentials (open_notebook/utils/encryption.py).
-- Lives in the shared `open_notebook` singleton-records table alongside
-- default_models/content_settings/provider_configs (see migrations 1, 11).

UPSERT open_notebook:drive_connection CONTENT {
    access_token: NONE,
    refresh_token: NONE,
    token_expiry: NONE,
    account_email: NONE,
    connected_at: NONE
};
